+Executive one-pager: Autonomy Controls and Requirements
+======================================================
+
+Goal
+----
+Define the organizational controls required to increase automation/autonomy safely in Aegis and explain what the platform will do automatically, what requires human approval, and the emergency rollback policy.
+
+Key decisions & requirements
+1. Hardware hard gate (Required)
+   - CI enforces presence of real hardware for critical branches (REQUIRE_REAL_HARDWARE=1).
+   - Rationale: prevent simulated CI from masking hardware regressions.
+2. SME signoff & proof policy
+   - High-priority invariants require SME signoff and proof artifacts before promotion.
+   - Automated issue creation and triage (daily) ensures visibility of outstanding proofs/signoffs.
+3. Safe autopilot policy for low-risk promotions
+   - Low-risk models meeting policy thresholds (e.g., F1 >= 0.90, p99 latency <= 50ms) receive an automated promotion event.
+   - Medium/high-risk models require human approval via issue/PR workflow.
+4. Secrets & signing
+   - KMS/OIDC roles must be provisioned; all signing in CI uses short-lived credentials.
+   - Langflow and vendor connectors must use Vault-backed secrets; UI must not store keys.
+5. Billing guard & quotas
+   - Billing reconciliation must be enabled and quotas set before broad TPU/QPU usage.
+6. SRE readiness
+   - Quarterly oncall drills and monthly long-load tests required before increasing automation scope.
+7. Emergency rollback policy
+   - Auto-promotion must be reversible: allow one-click rollback in registry and require an incident ticket if auto-promoted model is rolled back.
+
+What the platform will do automatically
+- Auto-generate issues for missing SME signoffs and proofs nightly.
+- Auto-promote low-risk models that pass signed-evidence checks and autopilot policy.
+- Block CI and promotions if the hardware hard gate fails when REQUIRE_REAL_HARDWARE=1.
+
+What requires human approval
+- Promotion of medium/high-risk models.
+- Acceptance of high-priority formal proofs and policy exceptions.
+- Provisioning of critical hardware and billing increases.
+
+Executive ask
+- Approve KMS/OIDC provisioning and GitHub Actions permissions (GITHUB_TOKEN) for automation.
+- Approve budget for initial device provisioning (one representative for each target).
+- Provide commitment to SME sprints to close top-10 invariants in 90 days.
+
+Metrics to track
+- Number of auto-promotions per week and rollback rate.
+- Time-to-approval for medium/high-risk promotions.
+- Number of SME outstanding invariants and average age.
+- Cost per promoted model (daily/weekly).
+
